    "title": "Freeport Athletics reports varsity and JV game results for October 7, 2025",
    "text": "Sarah Hasken Principal at Freeport High School | Official Website\nSarah Hasken Principal at Freeport High School | Official Website\nFreeport Athletics reported results from several varsity and junior varsity sports competitions on October 7, 2025, highlighting outcomes for the school's soccer, flag football, and volleyball teams.\nThe official Freeport Athletics account posted that \"Soccer Boys Varsity loses to Guilford with a final score of 0 - 3.\" on October 8, 2025. Shortly after, the account shared another update: \"Girls Varsity Flag Football loses to Round Lake with a final score of 0 - 24.\" The series of updates concluded with a positive result for one team: \"Volleyball Girls Junior Varsity defeats East with a final score of 25-21, 25-16.\"\nFreeport High School serves students in grades 9 through 12 in Freeport and Stephenson County. According to the Illinois Report Card, the school had an enrollment of 1,084 students during the 2019-2020 academic year (source). Grade 10 had the highest concentration of students at 24.2 percent (Illinois Report Card). Demographically, the student body was composed of approximately 50.5 percent white students, 24.2 percent black students, and 11.4 percent Hispanic students in that same year (Illinois Report Card).",
